cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the derived outputs, please cite the associated manuscript."
title: "Neither a Hierarchy nor a Bridging Elite: The Conceptual Architecture of the High-Performance Sport Ecosystem"
abstract: >-
  Replication repository for a falsification test of the structural assumption behind
  the nine-pillar (SPLISS) model of high-performance sport. Three predictions of a
  vertical architecture were specified in advance and tested against a concept network
  built from 448 Scopus documents (2013-2025). None produced the vertical picture and two
  produced nothing at all. What survives is a segmented field with a technical centre
  and diffuse integration. Includes a degree-controlled bridge analysis showing that the
  standard measure of integrative position is substantially a measure of how common a
  word is, and a manuscript verifier that fails the build on any untraceable statistic,
  unresolved citation or word-count disagreement.
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mahsatorabi/high-performance-sport-ecosystem-architecture"

# Bibliographic records retrieved from Scopus are NOT redistributed (see README).
# Derived outputs (tables, figures, verification files): CC BY 4.0

keywords:
